{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Final debug report before merge\n\nProblem: unrelated nested conftest changes selected all seven mutation shards, wasting contentious Ubuntu runner time without loading those fixtures.\n\nProven root cause: .github/mutation-shards.toml placed tests/**/conftest.py in global_support. scripts/mutation_gate.py treats any global_support match as all shards, while runtime tracing showed pytest loads only a selected test directory and ancestor conftests.\n\nProof: every configured shard was traced; the complete loaded set was tests/conftest.py plus five non-root ancestor conftests. tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py was absent. Across 97 completed Verify runs, seven candidate over-triggers consumed 19,353 runner-seconds, 322.6 runner-minutes, or 5.38 runner-hours. Pytest, Jest, and Nx all support dependency-accurate affected-test selection rather than sibling/global invalidation.\n\nTest: tests/scripts/test_mutation_gate.py::test_manifest_conftest_support_matches_selected_test_ancestry was RED against the original manifest, 1 failed in 0.17s, then GREEN after the held-out mapping fix, 1 passed in 0.56s. Removing a required interfaces dependency and adding stale Jira DC support each returned the final oracle to RED, 2 of 2 defect-seeded mutations killed. The complete mutation-gate file now passes 42 tests.\n\nFix: commit dd9f52a12d40acdbeeeab16e53d13aeb38ebef52 keeps only tests/conftest.py globally and assigns each non-root conftest to exactly the shards whose configured tests load it. The contract independently expands configured test files and directories, derives ancestor conftests, pins source/test and non-conftest globals, and checks exact selector ownership.\n\nScope and safety: the only selector consumer already distinguishes global_support from per-shard support. No caller depends on unrelated sibling conftests selecting every shard. No production capability, dependency, or test coverage was removed; no existing assertion was weakened. Exact shard-test union after updating to origin/main: 374 passed, 1 skipped, 1 existing warning in 23.07s. Config-check, Verify parity, lint, typecheck over 542 files, and diff checks passed.\n\nSiblings: repository sweep found no remaining tests/**/conftest.py invalidator. The manifest is the single configuration surface; no parity surface is missing.\n\nResidual risk and prevention: fixed in scope by the derived ancestry equality contract. If a future directory test entry gains nested collected tests and a conftest, expansion of test_*.py files makes that conftest an ancestor and fails closed until mapped. The single Gerrit change can be reverted to restore the recursive fail-safe if live evidence contradicts the trace.\n\nReplication: direct selector execution now returns zero shards for tests/external/live_jira_dc/conftest.py; unit conftest selects signing, compact-policy, and push-policy; interfaces conftest selects signing, reducer-processors, next-batch, gates, and validate; root tests/conftest.py still selects all seven. Gerrit change 1797 is pending both required votes: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1797."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786751763918423001,"uuid":"9c22b932-0892-4f95-b1be-f786e1df3b08"}